{"id":"f96b0ae85eb0a0b9599b5fe2b9f40c8cc2ac30a0","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"f96b0ae85eb0a0b9599b5fe2b9f40c8cc2ac30a0","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/ignore-lockfile-settings-checks.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/installing.deps-installer\": patch","+\"pnpm\": patch","+\"@pnpm/napi\": minor","+---","+","+Added the `ignoreLockfileSettingsChecks` install option to the programmatic API. When it is enabled, pnpm does not compare the `settings` in `pnpm-lock.yaml` with the current configuration, so a frozen install no longer fails with `ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH` and other installs no longer re-resolve because of a mismatch."],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/napi/src/install.rs","lines":["@@ -274,6 +274,7 @@ impl InstallShape {","                 frozen: self.frozen_lockfile,","                 prefer_frozen: self.prefer_frozen_lockfile,","                 ignore_manifest_check: options.ignore_package_manifest == Some(true),","+                ignore_settings_check: options.ignore_lockfile_settings_checks == Some(true),","                 disable_optimistic_repeat: mode.disable_optimistic_repeat_install(),","                 // The repeat-install fast path keys off `package.json` mtimes","                 // by default. NAPI installs use caller-supplied manifests"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/napi/src/install/options.rs","lines":["@@ -90,6 +90,10 @@ pub struct InstallOptions {","     /// pnpm's `pnpm fetch` semantics: the frozen path, no post-import","     /// linking, and no project lifecycle scripts.","     pub ignore_package_manifest: Option<bool>,","+    /// Do not compare the settings the lockfile records with the current","+    /// ones, so a mismatch neither fails a frozen install nor makes the","+    /// install resolve again.","+    pub ignore_lockfile_settings_checks: Option<bool>,","     pub node_version: Option<String>,","     pub engine_strict: Option<bool>,","     pub minimum_release_age: Option<u32>,"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/napi/src/install/tests.rs","lines":["@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@ fn install_options() -> InstallOptions {","         hoist_workspace_packages: None,","         enable_modules_dir: None,","         ignore_package_manifest: None,","+        ignore_lockfile_settings_checks: None,","         node_version: None,","         engine_strict: None,","         minimum_release_age: None,"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/napi/src/install/tests/lockfile.rs","lines":["@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@"," use super::{","-    EngineMode, HashMap, NodeApiProject, TestRegistry, install_options, run_install_inner,","+    EngineMode, HashMap, NodeApiProject, TestRegistry, install_options, install_options_for,","+    run_install_inner,"," };"," "," /// The lockfile must record `overrides` in declaration order — the","@@ -159,3 +160,37 @@ fn lockfile_version(lockfile: &str) -> Option<&str> {","                 .trim_matches(['\\'', '\"'])","         })"," }","+","+#[test]","+fn ignore_lockfile_settings_checks_keeps_a_lockfile_with_mismatched_settings() {","+    let temp_dir = tempfile::tempdir().expect(\"tempdir\");","+    let mut options = install_options_for(","+        temp_dir.path(),","+        \"project\",","+        serde_json::json!({ \"dependencies\": { \"@pnpm.e2e/foo\": \"100.0.0\" } }),","+    );","+    let lockfile_path = temp_dir.path().join(\"project/pnpm-lock.yaml\");","+    options.auto_install_peers = Some(true);","+    run_install_inner(&options, None, EngineMode::Install(None)).expect(\"seed install\");","+    let seeded = std::fs::read_to_string(&lockfile_path).expect(\"read lockfile\");","+","+    options.auto_install_peers = Some(false);","+    options.frozen_lockfile = Some(true);","+    let error = run_install_inner(&options, None, EngineMode::Install(None))","+        .expect_err(\"a frozen install rejects the mismatched settings\");","+    eprintln!(\"{error}\");","+    assert!(error.reason.contains(\"ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH\"));","+","+    options.ignore_lockfile_settings_checks = Some(true);","+    run_install_inner(&options, None, EngineMode::Install(None))","+        .expect(\"a frozen install ignoring the settings check\");","+","+    options.frozen_lockfile = None;","+    run_install_inner(&options, None, EngineMode::Install(None))","+        .expect(\"an install ignoring the settings check\");","+    assert_eq!(","+        std::fs::read_to_string(&lockfile_path).expect(\"read lockfile\"),","+        seeded,","+        \"the install must reuse the lockfile instead of resolving again\",","+    );","+}"],"additions":36,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/package-manager/src/install/lockfile_freshness.rs","lines":["@@ -131,10 +131,8 @@ async fn workspace_manifests_satisfy(","             scope: FreshnessScope {","                 ignore_manifest_check: check.ignore_manifest_check,","                 allow_missing_dependency_free_importers: true,","-                frozen_lockfile: false,","                 prune_stale_importers: true,","-                patches_only: false,","-                locked_registries: None,","+                ..FreshnessScope::default()","             },","         },","     )","@@ -260,10 +258,12 @@ pub(super) async fn try_fast_update_lockfile<Reporter: pnpm_reporter::Reporter>("," "," /// Which importers a freshness check may reason about, and how"," /// strictly. See [`check_lockfile_freshness`] for what each one admits.","-#[derive(Clone, Copy)]","+#[derive(Default, Clone, Copy)]"," pub(crate) struct FreshnessScope<'a> {","     /// Skip the per-importer specifier gate entirely.","     pub(crate) ignore_manifest_check: bool,","+    /// See [`crate::InstallLockfilePolicy::ignore_settings_check`].","+    pub(crate) ignore_settings_check: bool,","     /// Treat a project with no importer entry and no dependencies as","  